{"availability":"available","full":"amelia-m/lspc-weather","name":"lspc-weather","description":"Skydiving weather dashboard for the Lincoln Sport Parachute Club (Brown's Airport, NE69). Flags conditions against published USPA and FAA limits with the rule behind each. Always use your own judgment and follow USPA guidelines, drop zone policies and your S&TA's instructions.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-27T00:15:24Z","updated":"2026-10-10T04:25:41Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://amelia-m.github.io/lspc-weather/","topics":["dashboard","dropzone","github-pages","metar","nws","open-meteo","react","reactjs","skydiving","typescript","vite","weather","weather-app","weather-dashboard","winds-aloft"],"demo":"https://amelia-m.github.io/lspc-weather/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:17.803Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:17.803Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:17.803Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:17.803Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A skydiving weather dashboard for the Lincoln Sport Parachute Club (Brown's Airport, NE69) in Weeping Water, NE — tuned to the conditions that matter for jumpers and the club's Cessna 182 jump plane.","It consolidates the manual three-site routine (NOAA hourly forecast + usairnet cloud forecast + KPMV METAR) into one page, and adds winds aloft for freefall drift and density altitude for jump-plane climb performance.","In development — not endorsed or approved by USPA, LSPC, or any licensed professional. Advisory only. This dashboard flags conditions and cites guidance — it does not decide whether it's safe to jump. Every USPA, CFR and FAA citation here began as an AI recollection. Each has since been read at its source — the USPA SIM at uspa.org on 2026-09-22 (2-1 I, 2-2 and 4-7 again on 2026-10-08), the CFR sections, AIM 7-1-7 and FAA-P-8740-2 on 2026-